<h2 id="principles">0. Guiding principles (apply to every wave)</h2>
<p>Hard constraints carried from <code>.hermes.md</code> / <code>.ai-policy.md</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>No app restart, no edit to <code>comserv_server.pl</code></strong> (Shanta owns lifecycle). Verify with <code>perl -c</code>, targeted scripts, SQL inspection, <code>node --check</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Schema rule:</strong> Result class = single source of truth. Every table create/repair goes through the in-app schema-compare workflow (<code>/admin</code> → <code>create_table_from_result</code> / <code>sync_result_to_table</code>). NEVER hand-write DDL.</li>
    <li><strong>One doc mechanism:</strong> metadata in SQL (<code>documentationmetadataindex</code>); one reader <code>Comserv::Util::DocumentationConfig</code>. Cross-links live in file content; AI cites docs as <code>/Documentation/&lt;path&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>One schema mechanism:</strong> all DB grunt in <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> + <code>Util::Schema::*</code>. Zero raw SQL in controllers.</li>
    <li><strong>JS:</strong> modular files under <code>static/js/</code>, wired through <code>js_load.tt</code>, <code>data-*</code> delegation. No inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>. Theme via <code>var(--*)</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>No duplicate files; consolidate; stay in scope.</strong> Reuse before create.</li>
    <li><strong>File-size discipline:</strong> Controllers ≤2,000 soft; Util/Model/Result ≤800 soft.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="deps">1. Dependency map (what blocks what)</h2>
<pre class="masterplan-pre">
Schema System Plan ──────────────┬──&gt; Inventory/Order/Fulfillment (all schema)
        │                        ├──&gt; Voice Inspection P1 (audio_file_id cols)
        │                        ├──&gt; 3D Browse Gallery (showcase col)
        │                        ├──&gt; Herb Sign Generator (visibility col)
        │                        └──&gt; every other plan's schema changes
Documentation System Standard ───┬──&gt; Inventory Plan Phase 7 (doc obligations)
        │                        ├──&gt; AI2 Phase 4 (.md cross-links / citations)
        │                        └──&gt; all future doc writes
Herb Sign Generator (Phase 0) ──&gt; 3D Browse Gallery (openscad thumbnail reuse)
AI2 Migration (Phases 0-2 DONE) ─┬──&gt; local-chat.js V2 refactor
        │                        ├──&gt; Voice Inspection P3 (BeeMaster prompt)
        │                        └──&gt; AI2 Phase 4/5 cutover
Git Subsystem Refactor ──────────&gt; Deployment Workflow Plan (git_pull owner)
Deploy backup/rename fix ────────&gt; Deployment Workflow Plan (backup/rollback)
3D Browse Gallery (print queue) ─&gt; Inventory Plan Phase 6 (production dispatch)</pre>
<p><strong>Independent / parallelizable:</strong> Git refactor, Security hardening, Static::Simple absolute include_path.</p>

<h2 id="roadmap">2. The ordered roadmap (waves)</h2>

<h3 id="wave0">WAVE 0 — Establish the two "single source of truth" mechanisms</h3>
<p>Everything else references these. Do them first; both are largely additive / non-breaking, and independent of each other.</p>

<h4 id="w0-1">W0.1 — Schema System Plan</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/SchemaSystemPlan') %]">/Documentation/SchemaSystemPlan</a> (ACTIVE)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Done: problem framed; <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> exists; <code>/admin</code> endpoints work via DDL-from-Result; <code>INFRA_NAMING.md</code> states .20 primary / .198 backup.</li>
    <li>Remaining (blocks every other plan's schema work):
        <ul>
            <li><strong>G0</strong> resolve primary/backup + renormalize <code>db_config.json</code> priority (.20 explicit primary). <em>Blocking — do first.</em></li>
            <li><strong>G1</strong> extend <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code> with <code>create_table_from_result</code>, <code>sync_result_to_table</code>, <code>sync_to_backup</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>G2</strong> fold <code>/admin/backup</code> into the schema system.</li>
            <li><strong>G3</strong> strip ~42 raw-SQL lines from <code>Admin/SchemaComparison.pm</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>G4</strong> drift guard (report-only, one-click repair).</li>
            <li><strong>G5</strong> retire <code>script/sync_dev_from_production.pl</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Gate: G0 + G1 land so other plans can add columns via schema-compare.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w0-2">W0.2 — Documentation System Standard</h4>
<p>AI ref: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/plans/documentation-system-standard') %]">/Documentation/plans/documentation-system-standard</a> (.md, PLANNING 4/22)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Done: <code>STANDARD.md</code> written (S1–S7); summary in <code>.hermes.md</code>; superseded-plan banners; <code>load_from_db</code> additive reader added; <code>categories</code> JSON column pending (schema-compare).</li>
    <li>Remaining: Steps 5–22 — wire SQL live with JSON fallback, backfill 827 rows, delete JSON/META, build indexer (<code>script/index_documentation.pl</code>), wire deploy + cron, prove <code>.md</code> cross-links + AI citations (Steps 15–18).</li>
    <li>Gate: Steps 15–18 done so Inventory Phase 7 + AI2 citations follow the standard.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="wave1">WAVE 1 — Stabilize production-visible defects (parallel, mostly independent)</h3>

<h4 id="w1-1">W1.1 — Deploy backup/rename fix</h4>
<p>AI ref: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/plans/deploy-backup-rename-fix') %]">/Documentation/plans/deploy-backup-rename-fix</a> (.md, INVESTIGATION DONE; fix identified)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Remaining: 2-file, 4-line naming edit in <code>Comserv/docker-compose.yml</code> + <code>DockerDeploy.pm</code> (standardize <code>comserv2-web-staging/dev</code> → <code>comserv-web-*</code>), + the backup-by-<code>docker commit</code> fix (compose destroys <code>docker rename</code> backups). <strong>Gated on user approval + build finished</strong>. One-time <code>docker rename</code> of running <code>comserv2-web-*</code> containers.</li>
    <li>Gate: before any deploy-reliant plan assumes backups work.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w1-2">W1.2 — Git Subsystem Refactor (finish)</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/GitSubsystemRefactorPlan') %]">/Documentation/GitSubsystemRefactorPlan</a> (A / A2 / A3 / C DONE)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Done: duplicate route removed; V2 CSS (<code>admin-*</code> components); <code>chdir</code> class-of-bug fixed; <code>Comserv::Util::Git</code> service with whitelisted <code>git -C</code> runner; read + write helpers ported; dashboard skeleton; G.1/G.2/G.5/G.10/G.11 done.</li>
    <li>Remaining: <strong>B</strong> (centralise path — largely delivered early by A3), <strong>D</strong> (chained auth base), <strong>E</strong> (read-only parsers + partials), <strong>F.5/F.8/F.9</strong> (software-card include, convert 6 legacy templates to <code>admin-*</code>, in-browser check), <strong>G.3/G.4/G.6</strong> (safe pull, branch switch, write-safety contract).</li>
    <li>Gate: D/E/F done before Deployment Workflow Plan reuses git_pull owner.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w1-3">W1.3 — Security Hardening Free Stack</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/security_hardening_free_stack') %]">/Documentation/security_hardening_free_stack</a> (tools installed)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Done: gitleaks pre-commit hook; <code>security_scan.sh</code> unified scan; trivy image scan opt-in.</li>
    <li>Remaining: remediate <code>cpan-audit</code> advisories (CryptX, Catalyst Session/Auth, DBI, Starman, …) via <code>cpanm</code> upgrades, tracked through the existing error-audit / todo workflow. Can run in background.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w1-4">W1.4 — Static::Simple absolute include_path (defence-in-depth)</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Cross-cutting hardening flagged in Git plan A3.4 / H.6. Three live <code>chdir</code> bugs remain outside Git: <code>Admin.pm:463</code>, <code>Coding.pm:102</code>, <code>ProxyManager.pm:2160</code> — same restart-required CSS/JS 404 class.</li>
    <li>Fix: one line in <code>Comserv.pm</code> — <code>include_path =&gt; [ $c-&gt;path_to('root') ]</code> (absolute) so no <code>chdir</code> anywhere can 404 all assets. Touches core app config; its own reviewed commit.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="wave2">WAVE 2 — Chat / AI unification (large, JS-heavy; unblocks voice features)</h3>

<h4 id="w2-1">W2.1 — AI2 Migration (Phases 3–5) + local-chat.js V2 refactor (combined "Chat Unification")</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/ai2_migration_plan') %]">/Documentation/ai2_migration_plan</a> (Phases 0–2 DONE)</li>
    <li>AI ref: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/plans/local-chat-v2-refactor') %]">/Documentation/plans/local-chat-v2-refactor</a> (.md, NOT STARTED)</li>
    <li>Internal order:
        <ol>
            <li><strong>AI2 Phase 3</strong> — port <code>Model::AI::Chat</code> → <code>Model/AI2/Chat.pm</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>local-chat.js V2</strong> — extract Voice / Support / Page-context into <code>static/js/ai-chat/{voice,support,page-context}.js</code> + <code>index.js</code>; theme sweep; <code>node --check</code> each.</li>
            <li><strong>AI2 Phase 4</strong> — extract inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> from <code>ai2/index.tt</code> → <code>static/js/ai2/ai-chat-page.js</code>; run <code>python3 scripts/verify_js_v2.py</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>AI2 Phase 5</strong> — cutover v1→v2 (keep v1 until parity).</li>
        </ol>
    </li>
    <li>Why combined: the V2 refactor IS the JS half of AI2 Phase 4 — one rewrite, not two.</li>
    <li>Gate: done before Voice Inspection.</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w2-2">W2.2 — Voice Inspection Plan</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/VoiceInspectionPlan') %]">/Documentation/VoiceInspectionPlan</a> (ACTIVE)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Depends on: Schema System (W0.1) for P1 columns; AI2 (W2.1) for BeeMaster prompt + chat JS voice module.</li>
    <li>Order: <strong>P1</strong> link inspection↔voice/transcript (schema-compare) → <strong>P2</strong> fix <code>voice_recordings</code> double-row + pairing (B1/B2) → <strong>P3</strong> per-box/frame capture + standalone feeding action → <strong>P4</strong> queen health graph (chart JS) → <strong>P5</strong> frame inventory lifecycle.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="wave3">WAVE 3 — 3D / Sign / Shop foundation (depends on Schema; enables Inventory)</h3>

<h4 id="w3-1">W3.1 — Herb Sign Generator (remaining)</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/HerbSignGeneratorPlan') %]">/Documentation/HerbSignGeneratorPlan</a> (Phase 0 + A DONE)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Done: openscad service container (8083); <code>Util::SignGenerator</code> + <code>Controller::SignGenerator</code>; STL/PDF/JSON stored; <code>printing_3d_models</code> row per sign. <em>The openscad service built here is reused by 3D Browse Gallery.</em></li>
    <li>Remaining: browse shows stored sign PDF + populate <code>thumbnail_url</code>; single 3MF multi-object export; sign list UI + reprint; <code>printing_3d_jobs</code> integration; queue routing (next-available printer, Moonraker adapter).</li>
</ul>

<h4 id="w3-2">W3.2 — 3D Browse Gallery Plan</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3dBrowseGalleryPlan') %]">/Documentation/3dBrowseGalleryPlan</a> (PLANNING)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Depends on: Schema System (W0.1) for <code>showcase</code> column; openscad service (W3.1, done) for thumbnails.</li>
    <li>Build: role-driven routing (<code>/3d/browse</code> = farm console); STL thumbnail util (<code>Util::ModelThumbnail</code>) reusing openscad <code>/render_thumb</code>; <code>showcase</code> flag via schema-compare; reuse Shop as storefront; <code>/3d/store</code> advertising landing; order flow stock-aware filament + auto queue shortfall.</li>
    <li>Gate: print queue established here feeds Inventory Phase 6.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="wave4">WAVE 4 — Inventory / Order / Fulfillment (largest track)</h3>

<h4 id="w4-1">W4.1 — Inventory / Order / Fulfillment Plan</h4>
<p>Route: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/InventoryOrderFulfillmentPlan') %]">/Documentation/InventoryOrderFulfillmentPlan</a> (PLANNING, reviewed)</p>
<ul>
    <li>Depends on: Schema System (W0.1) for all §8 columns; 3D Browse Gallery (W3.2) print queue for Phase 6; existing accounting (CoA/GL/Invoice) + Payment (PayPal extraction).</li>
    <li>Internal gates (sub-plans must be approved before their phase):
